                        </tr>
                        <tr>
                           <td>The PSA value is elevated above the normal range for females; however, PSA is not typically relevant in female patients, as it is a marker for prostate tissue. This result may indicate a pre-analytical or clerical error, or rarely, ectopic PSA production. Clinical correlation and verification of the test and patient identity are recommended.</td>
